      "link": "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2026/aug/14/world-war-two-memorial-dc-vandalism",
      "description": "<p>Suspect faces two felony charges after memorial filled with bubbles and spray-paint reading ‘Clean hands Dirty $’</p><p>A woman was arrested on Friday morning in connection with the vandalization of the National World War Two Memorial on the National Mall in <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/washington-dc\">Washington DC</a>, the capital’s federal prosecutor announced.</p><p>Jeanine Pirro, the US attorney for the District of Columbia, announced mid-morning that a suspect was in custody and had been charged with federal crimes.</p> <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2026/aug/14/world-war-two-memorial-dc-vandalism\">Continue reading...</a>",
